  "capability": "identity",
  "operation": "verify_password",
  "conformance_level": "MUST",
  "spec_section": "docs/identity.md#lifecycle",
  "description": "User status is honoured at authentication and issuance time. Asserts ONLY accepted text: `docs/identity.md` \u00a7Lifecycle \u2014 a `suspended` user 'cannot authenticate' (and a `revoked` user is terminal); ADR 0016 \u00a7Constraints \u2014 `createPat` requires a non-revoked user, and PATs auto-revoke when their owner is revoked; `docs/identity.md` \u00a7PAT lifecycle \u2014 revoked tokens fail `verifyPatToken` with `PatRevokedError`. Every refusal arm is paired with a reinstate-and-succeed arm (the known positive: suspension is reversible, so the gate must be evaluated at verify/issue time, not by cascade). NOT asserted here (needs accepted text first, pending a spec clarification): refusing `createPat`/`createShare` for a SUSPENDED user. ERROR-NAME PROVENANCE: `PatRevokedError` is pinned by accepted text. `InvalidCredentialError` for `verifyPassword` follows `docs/identity.md` \u00a7Legacy migration step 2 (the named verifyPassword failure) and avoids a user-status oracle. `PreconditionError` for issuing to a non-active user (`createSession`, `createPat`) follows existing SDK precedent (Node createSession, PHP createPat) \u2014 PROVISIONAL, to be pinned by a pending spec clarification. The error for verifying a SUSPENDED owner's PAT (`InvalidPatTokenError`, conflated so status is not disclosed) is likewise PROVISIONAL. SCOPE (interpretation of accepted text): refusing `createSession` for a suspended user is IN scope \u2014 identity.md \u00a7Lifecycle requires a suspended user's active sessions be terminated on the transition and says the user 'cannot authenticate'; issuing a new session is the authenticated outcome, so none may be issued while suspended. This is distinct from the excluded suspended-user issuance of PATs/shares, which the accepted text does not cover. PAT CASCADE: the vector asserts ADR 0016 \u00a7Constraints' behaviour ('PATs auto-revoke when their owner is revoked'); the text is inconsistent about WHERE the cascade lives (0016 names `cascadeRevokeSubject`, which authorization.md defines as a tuple delete; identity.md \u00a7Operations lists revokeUser's cascades without PATs) \u2014 noted for reconciliation. Harness op `revoke_user` MUST invoke only the SDK's user-revocation operation (`revokeUser`), with no extra cascade call, so the vector tests that revoking a user is sufficient. Harness op `reinstate_user` maps to `reinstateUser`.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "id": "user_status.verify_password.suspended_refused",
      "description": "A suspended user's correct password is refused.",
      "users": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "op": "create_user_with_password_credential",
          "input": {
            "identifier": "sus@example.com",
            "password": "long-enough-password-for-floor"
          },
          "captures": {
            "usr_id": "user.id"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "suspend_user",
          "input": {
            "usr_id": "{usr_id}"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "verify_password",
          "input": {
            "identifier": "sus@example.com",
            "password": "long-enough-password-for-floor"
          },
          "expected": {
            "error": "InvalidCredentialError"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "user_status.verify_password.reinstated_ok",
      "description": "Known positive: suspend then reinstate; the correct password verifies.",
      "users": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "op": "create_user_with_password_credential",
          "input": {
            "identifier": "back@example.com",
            "password": "long-enough-password-for-floor"
          },
          "captures": {
            "usr_id": "user.id"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "suspend_user",
          "input": {
            "usr_id": "{usr_id}"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "reinstate_user",
          "input": {
            "usr_id": "{usr_id}"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "verify_password",
          "input": {
            "identifier": "back@example.com",
            "password": "long-enough-password-for-floor"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "user_status.verify_password.revoked_refused",
      "description": "A revoked user's correct password is refused.",
      "users": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "op": "create_user_with_password_credential",
          "input": {
            "identifier": "gone@example.com",
            "password": "long-enough-password-for-floor"
